# Valgrind suppressions for Micro-Vocal Lab (nightly memory-check workflow).
#
# Scope: third-party fontconfig internals only. The Slint font stack
# (fontique) loads fontconfig once; fontconfig (a) asks for per-script
# character sets through FcCharSetAddChar and (b) parses its system config
# XML through libexpat — both allocate caches/trees that fontconfig keeps
# for the process lifetime and frees only in FcFini(), which the font stack
# never calls; the OS reclaims them at exit. Reviewed against the Phase 5
# runs: 336 B definite+indirect in the charset caches, 256 B direct + 64 B
# indirect in the config-parse tree — zero first-party records. These rules
# keep the gate on real regressions in Micro-Vocal Lab code (DSP, buffers,
# app state).
{
   fontconfig-charset-cache
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   fun:FcCharSetAddChar
}
{
   fontconfig-config-parse
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   fun:XML_ParseBuffer
   ...
}
